{"id": "EUVD-2026-76266", "enisaUuid": "9487fc16-6b97-37e1-b5e0-25ed7809fe0c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtlwifi: rtl8192du: check QoS TID before indexing tids\n\nrtl92du_tx_fill_desc() uses ieee80211_get_tid() to read the QoS TID\nfrom the 802.11 header and then uses it as an index into\nsta_entry->tids[]. ieee80211_get_tid() returns the low 4-bit QoS TID\nvalue, so the result can be in the range 0..15.\n\nrtlwifi only allocates MAX_TID_COUNT entries for sta_entry->tids[], and\nMAX_TID_COUNT is 9. A QoS TID greater than 8 therefore indexes past the\naggregation state array. Keep the default RTL_AGG_STOP state for\nout-of-range TIDs, matching rtl92cu_tx_fill_desc().\n\nThis issue was detected by our static analysis tool and confirmed by\nmanual audit. UBSAN validation for the same bug pattern reports an\narray-index-out-of-bounds access with index 10 for type\n'rtl_tid_data [9]'.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:27", "baseScore": 7.6, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e327f14e1c43e175bf530f9165b2cadff308553", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c0b374e12d52af23ca741728db31091677cf9dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42785f7e8d31540e6172bbcf08a7cc3cae1086f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed4f05d9f2f42fd866f55108db8123eefcc5fb33"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80943", "GHSA-8f9m-rj4x-3w9p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "17b435ac-35e3-3217-9d0a-18e8a3d11806", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "23eb8cf1-2743-3248-bf3f-babf57f57f1f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "3474065b-413e-3861-807e-49a7416b1647", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "4d7f6bb1-6400-390c-9333-109f84a018ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "540166eb-d6c5-3a50-8a8e-3a2f03b1e8d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8321424134a400a5e3eb39f9acca6bc6946ff447 <ed4f05d9f2f42fd866f55108db8123eefcc5fb33"}, {"id": "8cdef93c-2716-3930-b1b0-57ccada044c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8321424134a400a5e3eb39f9acca6bc6946ff447 <42785f7e8d31540e6172bbcf08a7cc3cae1086f8"}, {"id": "93eee019-26db-317a-8af0-a159721bb591", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8321424134a400a5e3eb39f9acca6bc6946ff447 <6e327f14e1c43e175bf530f9165b2cadff308553"}, {"id": "dacd2cca-6867-36dc-b94c-809e86ff1e73", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8321424134a400a5e3eb39f9acca6bc6946ff447 <0c0b374e12d52af23ca741728db31091677cf9dc"}, {"id": "ece14907-1cc9-3147-93ad-e946b77b8c2e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "f4b21ffc-81d9-3b2e-b89d-72699e04f93a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "640254a7-f1fd-340b-8fda-ee7ecd392c3b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}